---
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader.astro';
import { missingData } from '@/data/site';
import { withBase } from '@/lib/paths';
---

<Layout
  title="Cookies and browser storage · draft"
  description="Draft audit of RAG-Ladder’s cookies, sessionStorage, localStorage, GitHub star-count cache and conditional Cloudflare Turnstile requests. No analytics is enabled."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="LEGAL / DRAFT FOR OWNER REVIEW"
    title="A small amount of session storage."
    description="The implementation uses tab-scoped credentials to resume a live demo. It has no advertising or analytics storage. The owner must verify the final Cloudflare deployment."
  />
  <Section eyebrow="STORAGE NOTICE" class="page-section prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        <strong>Draft for owner review.</strong> {missingData.contact.label}.
        This is a source-code audit, not a claim about uninspected deployment
        settings.
      </p>
    </div>
    <h2>Application storage audit</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Storage</th>
            <th>Current use</th>
            <th>Lifetime</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Application cookies</td>
            <td>
              None. Session access is sent only with requests to the demo
              service.
            </td>
            <td>Not applicable</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>sessionStorage</td>
            <td>
              Naive or Intermediate session access and metadata, returned
              limits, expiry and optional pending job ID. No file contents or
              chat transcript.
            </td>
            <td>
              This tab’s session, or until the app clears an
              ended/invalid/expired session.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>localStorage</td>
            <td>
              <code>rag-ladder:github-stars:v1</code>: the repository’s public
              star count and the time it was fetched.
            </td>
            <td>
              Reused for one hour, then refreshed; kept until you clear site
              data.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Page memory</td>
            <td>Selected files, visible questions/answers and mock state.</td>
            <td>
              Until reload, page navigation or session end clears the interface.
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h2>Cloudflare Turnstile</h2>
    <p>
      The live try pages load Cloudflare’s challenge script from
      challenges.cloudflare.com only after you accept the data notice. It can
      load a third-party iframe and make challenge-related requests.
      Verification requires the challenge response and network information. Mock
      mode does not load Turnstile.
    </p>
    <p>
      Turnstile itself does not require a pre-clearance cookie to issue a token.
      A separately configured Cloudflare pre-clearance or other edge security
      feature may set cookies. This frontend does not enable pre-clearance; the
      owner must inspect actual edge settings and browser behavior before
      finalizing this notice. See{' '}
      <a
        href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-challenges/concepts/clearance/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="underline"
      >
        Cloudflare’s clearance documentation
      </a>{' '}
      and{' '}
      <a
        href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="underline"
      >
        privacy addendum
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <h2>GitHub</h2>
    <p>
      The header links to the public repository and shows its star count. Your
      browser requests the count from the GitHub API (api.github.com) and stores
      only the number and a timestamp in localStorage, reused for one hour. No
      GitHub access token is included in the frontend.
    </p>
    <h2>No analytics or consent banner</h2>
    <p>
      No analytics, advertising, personalization or session-replay service is
      enabled. The current app-owned persistent storage is used only to keep the
      live demo session accessible within its tab. There is no consent banner in
      this implementation. Adding analytics or other storage requires a new
      owner review.
    </p>
    <h2>Clearing storage</h2>
    <p>
      “End session” requests live-data cleanup and removes the saved session
      record once confirmed. Clearing browser storage alone loses your local
      credentials and does not immediately delete server data; server expiry and
      cleanup still apply. Read the{' '}
      <a href={withBase('/privacy/')} class="underline">
        privacy draft
      </a>{' '}
      for those deletion limits.
    </p>
  </Section>
</Layout>
